---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { profile } from '../content/site';
---
<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description="What this site collects and stores. The short answer is almost nothing." lede="What this site collects, what it stores, and who can see what. The short answer is almost nothing.">
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>This website collects no personal information. There are no accounts, no forms, no comments, no ads and no analytics or tracking tools. It does not store anything in your browser.</p>
  <p>This policy applies to aaryavsharma-portfolio.vercel.app only. My textbooks and project websites are separate sites with their own notes.</p>
  <h2>Who I am</h2>
  <p>This site is run by Aaryav Sharma, a high school student in Apple Valley, Minnesota, United States. It is a personal portfolio, not a business. You can reach me at <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>.</p>
  <h2>What I collect</h2>
  <p>Through the website itself, nothing. It does not ask you to type in your name, email or any other detail, and it has no sign-up or login.</p>
  <p>If you email me, I will receive your email address and whatever you write. I use it only to reply to you. I do not sell it, share it or add it to any list. I delete emails when I no longer need them.</p>
  <h2>What my hosting company can see</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted by Vercel Inc. Like any web host, Vercel keeps ordinary server logs, such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you request, to keep the service secure and running. I do not use those logs to identify visitors. Vercel’s handling of that data is covered by its own <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>This site sets no cookies and saves nothing in your browser’s storage. Details are on the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>This site links to places that are not run by me, including my project sites on vercel.app, the SASA and EDAN websites, GitHub, Google Drive (for my resume) and my textbooks on GitHub Pages. Those sites have their own privacy practices and may set their own cookies or use analytics, so please read their policies.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13. If you believe a child has emailed me personal information, tell me and I will delete it.</p>
  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>Because the site does not collect personal data, there is nothing for me to access, correct or delete from the site itself. If you have emailed me and want me to delete your message or tell you what I kept, write to <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> and I will do it. Depending on where you live, laws such as the GDPR or the California Consumer Privacy Act may give you extra rights, and you can use them by emailing me.</p>
  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>The site is delivered over HTTPS and uses security headers such as a strict content security policy. No system is perfectly secure, but because the site holds no personal data, there is very little to protect.</p>
  <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, I will update the date at the top. Questions go to <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
